    "gold_text": "Record: 37-45, 10th in NBA Western Conference Last Game: L 96-111 at PHO Coach: Steve Kerr (37-45) Executive: Mike Dunleavy PTS/G: 114.6 (22nd of 30) Opp PTS/G: 115.2 (14th of 30) SRS: -0.34 (20th of 30) Pace: 99.0 (19th of 30) Off Rtg: 115.0 (18th of 30) Def Rtg: 115.6 (17th of 30) Net Rtg: -0.6 (20th of 30) Expected W-L: 40-42 (20th of 30) Preseason Odds: Championship +2500, Over-Under 47.5 Arena: Chase Center Attendance: 740,624 (16th of 30) Roster No. Player Pos Ht Wt Birth Date Birth Exp College 2 Brandin Podziemski SG 6-4 205 February 25, 2003 us US 2 Illinois, Santa Clara 0 Gary Payton II SG 6-2 195 December 1, 1992 us US 9 Oregon State 3 Will Richard SG 6-3 206 December 24, 2002 us US R Belmont, Florida 15 Gui Santos PF 6-7 185 June 22, 2002 br BR 2 23 Draymond Green PF 6-6 230 March 4, 1990 us US 13 Michigan State 21 Quinten Post PF 7-0 238 March 21, 2000 nl NL 1 Mississippi State, Boston College 61 Pat Spencer PG 6-2 205 July 4, 1996 us US 2 Loyola (MD), Northwestern 4 Moses Moody SG 6-5 211 May 31, 2002 us US 4 Arkansas 8 De'Anthony Melton PG 6-2 200 May 28, 1998 us US 7 USC 20 Al Horford C 6-8 240 June 3, 1986 do DO 18 Florida 30 Stephen Curry PG 6-2 185 March 14, 1988 us US 16 Davidson 10 Jimmy Butler SF 6-6 230 September 14, 1989 us US 14 Tyler Junior College, Marquette 33 Malevy Leons (TW) SF 6-9 210 September 23, 1999 nl NL 1 Mineral Area College, Bradley 18 LJ Cryer (TW) PG 6-1 202 October 9, 2001 us US R Baylor, Houston 7 Kristaps Porziņģis C 7-2 240 August 2, 1995 lv LV 9 19 Nate Williams (TW) SG 6-5 205 February 12, 1999 us US 3 Buffalo 31 Seth Curry SG 6-1 185 August 23, 1990 us US 11 Liberty, Duke 28 Charles Bassey C 6-10 230 October 28, 2000 ng NG 4 Western Kentucky Injury Report Player Team Update Description Jimmy Butler Golden State Warriors Tue, Jan 20, 2026 Out For Season (Knee) - Butler's injury from Monday (Jan. 19) Night's game involves a torn right ACL and he will be out for the rest of the season, as per Shams Charania of ESPN. Moses Moody Golden State Warriors Mon, Mar 23, 2026 Out For Season (Knee) - The Warriors reported guard Moses Moody has been diagnosed with a torn patellar tendon in his left knee, and is out for the season. Quinten Post Golden State Warriors Sat, Apr 4, 2026 Out (Foot) - The Warriors announced on Saturday (Apr. 4) that Post will be re-evaluated next week. Assistant Coaches and Staff Seth Cooper Assistant Coach/Director of Player Development Bruce Fraser Assistant Coach Ron Adams Assistant Coach Chris DeMarco Assistant Coach Nicholas Kerr Assistant Coach Khalid Robinson Assistant Coach Kris Weems Assistant Coach Jacob Rubin Assistant Coach Jerry Stackhouse Assistant Coach Terry Stotts Assistant Coach Anthony Vereen Assistant Coach Frequently Asked Questions What is the Golden State Warriors' record? The Golden State Warriors have a record of 37-45. When is the Golden State Warriors' next game? The Golden State Warriors' next game is vs. Where do the Golden State Warriors play? The Golden State Warriors play at Chase Center in San Francisco, CA. Who did the Golden State Warriors draft in 2025? In 2025, the Golden State Warriors made 1 pick; Koby Brea with the 41st overall pick."
